+++ b/compiler/src/scanner/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+# Android standard library sources
+
+This directory vendors the complete, unchanged Android Open Source Project `java.util.Scanner` and `java.util.Spliterators` implementations. Scanner uses the standard AbstractSpliterator for its stream APIs. These are maintained OpenJDK-derived sources, not partial API emulations.
+
+- Repository: https://android.googlesource.com/platform/libcore/
+- Commit: `de876a01b29230b877c9f408348c38a90ee724a5`
+- Paths: `ojluni/src/main/java/java/util/Scanner.java`, `ojluni/src/main/java/java/util/Spliterators.java`
+- Scanner SHA-256: `6b5fc3fb48169d116c1cf3868f35e32b091695480950b3a0a6bfdbebfb5ab37d`
+- Spliterators SHA-256: `7363a624984c81e6a8c0a7ac72e43e360c86f6c92f3ccc9a55c87d43ca987066`
+- License: GPL version 2 with Classpath exception; original headers and LICENSE are preserved.
+
+Javac compiles the original sources into the SDK. ASM relocates both classes and their nested classes to the usual TeaVM classlib namespace for the runtime archive. TeaVM then performs its standard library substitution. The source implementations are not rewritten.
